WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:10.040
Vladimir Putin's re-election is certain.
Don't waste your time looking at his

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.429
carefully-scripted but sterile campaign
for clues to Russia's future. Instead,

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:17.730
look at the $327 billion dollar defense modernization

00:00:17.730 --> 00:00:23.519
program that Putin signed in Sochi on
November 27th after a non-stop, four day

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:28.170
session with Russia's top military brass.
This in a country where personal incomes

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:31.920
have been going down for four years,
growing poverty is a key problem, and

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.910
social protests are up 56 percent. But
that's exactly the point:

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:40.890
Russia is effectively at war. When he
signed the defense modernization program,

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:46.170
Putin called on all Russian enterprises –
private or state – to be ready to switch to

00:00:46.170 --> 00:00:50.579
military production "in a time of need" as
he put it in order to, again a quote,

00:00:50.579 --> 00:00:54.629
"efficiently neutralize" external threats.
The message is clear:

00:00:54.629 --> 00:00:59.520
Putin is a wartime president, and wartime
presidents are not to be replaced so

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:04.140
long as the war is going on. And Putin,
his propaganda machine, and his generals

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:07.740
will make sure that it is, and gets
hotter by the day.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:15.020
So what do you think will happen in Russia after Vladimir Putin's re-election in March 2018? Let us

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.960
know in your comments. Also, let us know
what other topics you'd like our

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:23.040
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:26.659
research and videos from AEI.

